      "updated": 1786126396501,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "    BeanFactory                 vs                 ApplicationContext\n\n1. lazy initialization                          2. eager initialization\nwhen getBeans is called                    beans are created as soon  \n then only its bean is created .           as application is started ,but\n                                                 bean with scope value singleton\n                                                 or prototype .\n\n2. provides basic features                 Advance features thus require                \nthus require less memory  .                 more memory . \n\n\n3. It supports only singleton              It supports all type of bean \nand prototype bean scope .                scope such as singleton, \n                                                  prototype, request, session etc .\n\n4. BeanFactory does not                   Event handling in application \nsupport event publication                   context is provided through\nfunctionality .                                 ApplicationEvent class and\n                                                  EventListener interface .\n\n5. Doesn't support annotaion .            Supports annotation based \n                                                  configuration .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "    BeanFactory                 vs                 ApplicationContext\n\n1. lazy initialization                          2. eager initialization\nwhen getBeans is called                    beans are created as soon  \n then only its bean is created .           as application is started ,but\n                                                 bean with scope value singleton\n                                                 or prototype .\n\n2. provides basic features                 Advance features thus require                \nthus require less memory  .                 more memory . \n\n\n3. It supports only singleton              It supports all type of bean \nand prototype bean scope .                scope such as singleton, \n                                                  prototype, request, session etc .\n\n4. BeanFactory does not                   Event handling in application \nsupport event publication                   context is provided through\nfunctionality .                                 ApplicationEvent class and\n                                                  EventListener interface .\n\n5. Doesn't support annotaion .            Supports annotation based \n                                                  configuration .",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
